esenting the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["los angeles", "california", "city life", "geography", "weather", "hiking", "mountains", "ocean", "neighborhoods", "crime", "politics", "woke culture", "earthquakes", "natural disasters", "risk prediction"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778537183.1908052, "duration_sec": 3.118842601776123, "validator_hotkey": "5DkzbwTnocecNohGP4aNVcHZfUgx8uA1MGQ4WB1u3kfi78gE", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "And she worries the agency will continue to lose officers to more steady jobs and fail to attract new talent, which, of course, is not a giant shock. Now, this is crazy talent. It's insanity. And it's happening because Democrats have decided that posturing over ICE is more important than basic safety standards and citizen protections all over the United States. The Senate Majority Leader John Thune is not wrong when he says that Democrats seem to believe that the current shutdown is good for their left wing base."], [0, "them it's all about politics and it always has been you go back to the fall shutdown the democrats shut the government down the whole government down for 46 days last fall and if you remember chuck schumer's statement that every day gets better for us and then you have brian shots a member of the democrat leadership and this shutdown saying we are very serene uh this is i mean i think they're just playing politics with this have been from the beginning"], [0, "They think it's really good with their base. Their left-wing base won't take yes for an answer. And so the Democrats are having a hard time taking yes for an answer. But they're going to have to because at some point people are realizing that it is the Democrats who are blockading and have been blockading funding the Department of Homeland Security now literally for 46 days."], [0, "Now, for some reason, Democrats seem to think they can just insult their way to political victory here. This is very simple. The Democrats are shutting down the Department of Homeland Security. Everyone knows this. All they have to do is pass a clean funding bill for DHS. But somehow Jimmy Kimmel is out there just randomly insulting the new DHS secretary, Mark Wayne Mullen, for the great crime of being a plumber."], [0, "Which is a weird take from Jimmy Kimmel, who was like a shock jock radio sports guy. Why is he commenting on this in this way? Also, I was informed that it's good that AOC was a bartender. So I guess it's bad that a man who was a senator is now running DHS because at one time he was a plumber. Rudy Giuliani might not be with us much longer, but..."], [0, "Don't worry, Trump's got a whole new generation of thinkers lined up, including his newly confirmed Secretary of Homeland Security, Mark Wayne, Chuck Mike, Bruce Dave Mullen. Maybe Mullen's better. He is the now former senator of Oklahoma. Before he was elected to the Senate, Mark Wayne Mullen was a low-level MMA fighter and a plumber. That's right. We have a plumber protecting us from terrorism now."], [0, "It worked for Super Mario. Why not Mark Wayne? But honestly, I mean, if Trump is going to keep picking these unqualified people to run the department, why not have more fun with it? I mean, next time, instead of Mark Wayne, how about Little Wayne for Homeland Security? Who is writing those quasi-jokes for Jimmy Kimmel? I can't imagine why his ratings are really, really, really terrible."], [0, "Again, I'm not sure why the fact that he was once a plumber and then was elected to the Senate makes him unfit to run DHS. That's a weird take. Well, most Democrats are actually going harder than this. Brandon Johnson, the ridiculous mayor of Chicago, actually debuted his own snowplow truck."], [0, "festooned with a banner that says on it, abolish ice. Get it? Because he's abolishing the actual material that is ice, but he also wants to abolish ice. Things are going amazing in the city of Chicago. To all of the residents who participated in our snowplow naming contest..."], [0, "keep speaking up in every way and any way that you can. I look forward to meeting with the Chicagoans who submitted the winning names and I look forward to seeing our city's pride our spirit and even yes our humor represent us again next year and so with that take a moment to"]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["News & Politics"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["politics", "government shutdown", "homeland security", "immigration", "border enforcement", "ice", "democrats", "republicans", "senate", "political rhetoric", "political satire", "television comedy", "public safety", "chicago", "workforce retention"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
