{"timestamp": 1778537799.3943238, "duration_sec": 1.6998987197875977, "validator_hotkey": "5DkzbwTnocecNohGP4aNVcHZfUgx8uA1MGQ4WB1u3kfi78gE", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "And yet, as we approach that 10-year mark, as we approach today, if you were to ask those same people, did you accomplish the happiness that you wanted? Have you arrived at the place that you were going? Many would say,"], [0, "No. And so this idea of change, of externally focused change, this desire for our circumstances around us to shift, this is what I want to focus on in today's episode. And more specifically, I want to talk to you about how we can change that focus and"], [0, "and perhaps find happiness in a different way. But first, I want to talk about today's sponsor, Linode. Linode is returning as a sponsor to Developer Tea, and they're providing you with $20 worth of credit, which is equivalent to four free months on Linode's platform."], [0, "Linode has 10 data centers worldwide, and plans start at just $5 a month. They have a seven-day money-back guarantee, so if you get started with Linode and in seven days you decide that you're not happy, you can get all of your money back. Of course, you can start for free, so"], [0, "There's essentially no risk. Linode has 24-7 friendly support, and they even have phone support available, and they have native SSD storage. All of it runs on a 40-gigabit internal network on top of Intel E5 processors."], [0, "With Linode, you can instantly deploy and manage an SSD server in the Linode cloud. You can get a server running in just seconds with your choice of Linux distribution, resources, and node location. Head over to linode.com slash developer T. That's Linode, L-I-N-O-D-E dot com slash developer T, all one word, and use the code developer T2018 when you check out for that $20 worth of credit."], [0, "Thank you again to Linode for sponsoring today's episode of Developer Tea and for providing listeners with credit on their platform. And so this fixation that we have on change, the idea that..."], [0, "Once I get something, or once something happens around me, or once that certain person starts acting in this different way, or once I cultivate this particular relationship, all of these things are kind of external effects."], [0, "They're a state of the world that's outside of us. And here's the problem with this. The problem is, as we have already mentioned, that as we approach that state, things tend to change. We tend to change our definition of what we believe the best state of the world could be."], [0, "And our happiness target kind of moves. And so even with a lot of work that we exert on the external world to try to manage it into a state that we want, we often end up not any happier than we were before."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Coding"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["happiness", "personal growth", "change", "life goals", "self improvement", "motivation", 